#TOTAL 200
#DIFFICULTY 1

*---------------------- EXTENDED HEADER FIELD
* Channels `97` and `98` are the two dynamic volume buses:
*
*   #xxx97 - BGM-side (autoplay / channel 01) bus volume
*   #xxx98 - playable-side (key sound) bus volume
*
* The token is a base-36 pair read as a 0..FF ratio of the original volume, so
* `FF` is unity, `80` is roughly half, and `01` is the quietest audible step.
* `00` is "no event" rather than silence, so it is never authored as a value.
*
* Both channels must stay out of the sample-trigger path - authoring a volume
* change must not itself make a sound - which is what makes a real chart worth
* having here rather than only the classifier unit tests.

#PLAYER 1
#LNTYPE 1
#VOLWAV 100

